thread:
maria: Heads up — we've seen 3 eviction waves in us-west-2 over the last 6 hours, all targeting the same instance types. Likely price pressure. Thinking we should expand the spot pool to include A10g, T4s, and some cheaper V100 families to spread risk.

sam: Agreed. The multi-instance approach reduced our outages before, but packing across shapes is messy. :thinking:

chris: What's our biggest blocker for mixing A100/A10/T4? Is it scheduling (GPU memory mismatch) or the model-side (OOMs)?

maria: Mostly scheduling. Right now our pod resource requests assume 48GB and get scheduled on A100s. If we add A10 (24GB) we need smarter bin packing or a different quota class. Also performance variability — A10 latency is worse for some models.

jin: We could add a new nodePool with lower-request flavors and auto-split the workload by priority. e.g. batch jobs -> T4/A10, latency-critical -> A100. Also use nodeSelector/taints to keep pods on compatible shapes.

sam: Another option: runtime-level device arbitration — have the inference runtime accept lower-VRAM instances by swapping to 8-bit quant models on those nodes. Might need model conversion pipeline automation.

maria: I like that. Two levers: 1) shape-aware scheduler + pod classes 2) runtime fallback to quantized variants. Both reduce evictions impact.

ops-bot: [alert] 2025-06-15T12:30:01Z detected 9 spot terminations in us-west-2a for instance-type g4dn.xlarge

chris: Are we ok with slightly higher p99 latency on fallback nodes? Product will accept occasional tail increases if throughput/cost improves.

maria: Product said yes as long as errors don't increase. We should add a QoS metric and circuit-breaker to failover to reserved capacity if error rate spikes.

jin: Drafted a quick autoscaler tweak — set mixedInstancesPolicy with capacity-optimized and diversify across families. Terraform snippet:

```
resource "aws_asg" "gpu_spot" {
  mixed_instances_policy {
    instances_distribution { on_demand_base_capacity = 1 }
    launch_template { ... }
    override { instance_type = "p4d.24xlarge" }
    override { instance_type = "g5.12xlarge" }
  }
}
```

sam: Nice. Also add eviction-aware drain hooks so we can checkpoint KV caches to s3 before node termination, reduces cold-start cost.

maria: Good call. I'll prototype two experiments: A) diversify instance pools with shape-aware scheduler, B) single pool + runtime quant fallback. We'll compare 7-day cost and sustained p99.

chris: Set up dashboards: cost per token by node-shape, eviction rate, p99 token latency. Share results next week. :thumbsup:

jin: I'll add the autoscaler PR and a KEP for scheduler changes.

maria: Thanks team — let's keep the rollout gradual and watch for correlated preemptions across AZs.
